@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Creating and Managing Projects";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Creating and managing projects in Azure DevOps is crucial for organizing and tracking work efficiently. Projects provide a structured environment for teams to collaborate on code, manage pipelines, and track development progress.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Step-by-Step Guide to Creating an Azure DevOps Project</h2>
        <p>Follow these steps to create a new project in Azure DevOps:</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Step 1: Access Azure DevOps</h4>
            <p>Navigate to <a href="https://dev.azure.com/" target="_blank">Azure DevOps</a> and sign in with your Microsoft account.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/create-project.png" alt="Create a New Project" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Creating a new project in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/project-settings.png" alt="Project Settings" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Project configuration options</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>Step 2: Create a New Project</h4>
            <p>Click on "New Project" and enter the project name. Choose the visibility (private or public), select a version control system (Git or TFVC), and choose the work item process (Agile, Scrum, CMMI).</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Managing an Azure DevOps Project</h2>
        <p>Once the project is created, you can manage various aspects such as repositories, pipelines, and work items.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>1. Managing Repositories</h4>
            <p>Azure Repos allows teams to store and manage source code efficiently. You can create branches, manage pull requests, and enforce branch policies.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/repos-overview.png" alt="Azure Repos" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Managing repositories in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/boards-overview.png" alt="Azure Boards" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Tracking work with Azure Boards</small></p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>2. Tracking Work Items</h4>
            <p>Azure Boards provides a project management system where teams can track work using backlog, sprints, and task boards.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row align-items-center mt-4">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <h4>3. Setting Up Pipelines</h4>
            <p>Azure Pipelines helps automate builds, testing, and deployments. You can define pipeline workflows using YAML or a visual editor.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="col-md-6 text-center">
            <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/media/pipelines-overview.png" alt="Azure Pipelines" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>CI/CD automation with Azure Pipelines</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Creating and managing projects in Azure DevOps provides a structured workflow for software development. With built-in tools for source control, project tracking, and automation, teams can efficiently collaborate and deliver high-quality software.
        </p>
        <p>
            The next step is to explore **Azure Repos** for version control and repository management.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-start mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("NavigatingAzureDevOpsUI", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Navigating Azure DevOps UI</a>
    </div>
</div>
